<title>MALAYSIA: SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-WORLD YOUTH CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of world youth</p>
<p>soccer championship matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>Group A:</p>
<p>Belgium 3  Malaysia 0 (halftime 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Belgium -- Gunter Van Handenhoven 8, 28, Gauthier Remacle 82</p>
<p>Uruguay 0 Morocco 0</p>
<p>Group B:</p>
<p>Brazil 10 South Korea 3 (halftime 6-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Brazil -- Fernandao Da Costa 19, 41, Adailton Martins 30,</p>
<p>32, 35, 38, 62, 68, Vinicius Da Silva 66, Junior Junior 80</p>
<p>South Korea --Lee Kwan Woo 55, Chung Seok Keun 71, Lee Jung</p>
<p>Ming 90</p>
<p>France 4  South Africa 2  (halftime 1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France -- David Trezequet 22, 61, Thierry Henry 82, Peter</p>
<p>Luccin 88</p>
<p>South Africa -- Moegamad Hartley 42, 90</p>
<p>Group C:</p>
<p>    Ghana 1   USA 0  (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer:</p>
<p>Peter Ofori-Quaye 33</p>
</text>
